      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Feeling like you lack control is an incredibly painful and disorienting place to be. When agency feels gone, focusing on the absolute smallest choices can sometimes help create a tiny spark of control. This could be as simple as choosing what you drink or what music you listen to, giving yourself a small act of self-direction. Even in the hardest moments, there are small ways you can assert yourself and care for that part of you that is suffering.",
      "source": "target",
